# EF migrations are immutable (user-owned)

The developer owns all EF migrations. The agent must not touch them.

## Forbidden

- Create, edit, rewrite, patch, delete, or "fix" any file under `**/Migrations/**`
  (migration `.cs`, `.Designer.cs`, `*ModelSnapshot.cs`)
- Run `dotnet ef migrations add|remove`, `dotnet ef database update`,
  `Add-Migration`, `Update-Database`, or apply efbundle
- Hand-write migration SQL/`Up`/`Down` as a substitute for `migrations add`

## Allowed

- Change Entity models and EF configuration only
- Tell the user the exact `dotnet ef ...` command to run (always include `--context` when multiple DbContexts exist)
- Diagnose apply failures and suggest alternatives that do **not** edit migration files
  (e.g. one-off SQL the user runs, or restoring a clean DB baseline)

## Exception

Only restore/copy a migration file when the user **explicitly** requests restoring that specific file from a known original in the same message.
